{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "92", "x": 0.9042195477562772, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.029523700847358492, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "C", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12334338960510077, "w": 0.020642617695827533, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "16", "x": 0.12582140429864574, "y": 0.15419533932580404, "w": 0.027866154287957533, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "As a result, coral reefs are often described as the 'rainforests of the sea', though", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.20388474892414815, "w": 0.8259468974052268, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "the comparison is dismissed by some naturalists, including David Attenborough.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.22435380991345355, "w": 0.8260117957009852, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "'People say you cannot beat the rainforest,' Attenborough has stated. 'But that is", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.24467455038740624, "w": 0.824842601127795, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "simply not true. You go there and the first thing you think is: where ... are the birds?", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.27497018501135945, "w": 0.8260553688063522, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Where are the animals? They are hiding in the trees, of course. No, if you want", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2952909254853121, "w": 0.8258814864846993, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "beauty and wildlife, you want a coral reef. Put on a mask and stick your head under", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3157599864746175, "w": 0.8267676096604343, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "the water. The sight is mind-blowing.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.33608070808787394, "w": 0.3832817735340649, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "D", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.39659796796367397, "w": 0.020642617695827533, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "17", "x": 0.12622454523262552, "y": 0.4274498799629847, "w": 0.02726143647917826, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Unfortunately, these majestic sights are now under very serious threat, with the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4773123175887762, "w": 0.825837503279517, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "most immediate problem coming in the form of thermal stress. Rising ocean", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.49763305806272884, "w": 0.8258594436196312, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "temperatures are triggering bleaching events that strip reefs of their colour and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5181021190520343, "w": 0.8263206008618452, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "eventually kill them. And that is just the start. Other menaces include ocean", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5384228595259869, "w": 0.8257940326991037, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "acidification, sea level increase, pollution by humans, deoxygenation and ocean", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5587435999999396, "w": 0.8262077208877061, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "current changes, while the climate crisis is also increasing habitat destruction. As", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5792126609892451, "w": 0.8265985460116101, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "a result, vast areas - including massive chunks of Australia's Great Barrier Reef -", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5995334014631978, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "have already been destroyed, and scientists advise that more than 90% of reefs", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6200024624525031, "w": 0.8260120007508928, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "could be lost by 2050 unless urgent action is taken to tackle global heating and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6403232029264558, "w": 0.8266957396678171, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "greenhouse gas emissions.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6606809858078542, "w": 0.2782625670218439, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Pearce-Kelly says that coral reefs have to survive really harsh conditions - wave", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6909396534671467, "w": 0.8268319953314237, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "erosion and other factors. And 'when things start to go wrong in the oceans, then", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.711408714456452, "w": 0.8258593410946774, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "corals will be the first to react. And that is exactly what we are seeing now. Coral", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7317294549304048, "w": 0.8264028258747967, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "reefs are dying and they are telling us that all is not well with our planet.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7520501954043575, "w": 0.7445832478531531, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "E", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8127157003527252, "w": 0.01882846426948971, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "18", "x": 0.12561982742384625, "y": 0.8435676500734285, "w": 0.028269295221937305, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "However, scientists are trying to pinpoint hardy types of coral that could survive", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8932818049052597, "w": 0.825968325120572, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "our overheated oceans, and some of this research will be carried out at London", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9137508658945651, "w": 0.8265471810097539, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Zoo. 'Behind our ... coral reef tank we have built laboratories where scientists will", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.9340716063685178, "w": 0.8259030167249982, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}